          {
            "kind": "heading",
            "id": "h",
            "text": "How the Northstar Workshop team runs a release review on Zoom",
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "t",
            "text": "12 February 2026. Customer story."
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "t-2",
            "text": "Northstar Workshop is a sixteen-person company building Atlas, a deterministic computer simulator. Every release passes through a thirty-minute review on Zoom with the release lead, two engineers and the support lead."
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "t-3",
            "text": "\"The rule is that the checklist is on screen the whole time,\" says engineering manager Priya Raman. \"We share the document, walk the items in order, and the release code only gets written down after everyone in the room has said yes.\""
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "t-4",
            "text": "The team records to the cloud so the postmortem, if there is one, can quote the review. AI Companion writes the action items into the team's chat channel before the call ends."
          },
          {
            "kind": "text",
            "id": "t-5",
            "text": "Their advice for small teams: keep the meeting short, keep the checklist boring, and make one person the owner."
          },
          {
            "kind": "link",
            "id": "northstar",
            "text": "Northstar Workshop",
            "url": "http://northstar.example/"
          },
